WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.168 --> 00:00:19.270
Dickon pushed Colin's wheelchair until they came to a spot in the garden filled with flowering trees.

2
00:00:20.451 --> 00:00:23.192
Mary and Dickon worked here and there as Colin watched.

3
00:00:24.293 --> 00:00:30.655
They brought him things to look at: green buds on a twig, a woodpecker's feather, the empty shell

4
00:00:30.675 --> 00:00:31.956
of a bird that had hatched.

5
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.541
Then Dickon pushed him slowly around the garden.

6
00:00:35.561 --> 00:00:39.643
"I wonder if we'll see the robin," said Colin.

7
00:00:39.663 --> 00:00:43.204
"Oh, you'll see him soon enough," said Dickon.

8
00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:47.746
"When the eggs hatch, he'll be busy bringing worms to his family."

9
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:50.127
Dickon pulled out his pipe.

10
00:00:51.348 --> 00:00:53.989
Before he could begin to play, Colin noticed something.

11
00:00:54.009 --> 00:00:56.770
"That's a very old tree over there."

12
00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.931
"Yes," Dickon said quietly.

13
00:01:00.431 --> 00:01:01.532
He glanced at Mary.

14
00:01:03.168 --> 00:01:06.351
"It looks as if a big branch broke off," said Colin.

15
00:01:06.371 --> 00:01:08.432
"I wonder how that happened."

16
00:01:08.452 --> 00:01:12.035
"It broke a long time ago," said Dickon.

17
00:01:12.055 --> 00:01:15.138
"Oh, look, here's the robin."

18
00:01:16.379 --> 00:01:18.901
Colin laughed as he watched the bird flying around.

19
00:01:20.142 --> 00:01:21.683
He forgot all about the tree.

20
00:01:23.905 --> 00:01:28.588
When they talked about it later, Mary told Dickon it was magic that the robin had appeared just

21
00:01:28.648 --> 00:01:32.872
then. They hadn't wanted to tell Colin about the horrible accident.

22
00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.661
"Mother thinks Colin's mother sometimes comes back to watch over him," Dickon had said.

23
00:01:38.681 --> 00:01:42.702
"Perhaps she set us to work and told us to bring him here."

24
00:01:44.343 --> 00:01:46.083
Mary wondered whether this could be true.

25
00:01:48.044 --> 00:01:51.985
There was no question, however, that being in the garden was doing Colin good.

26
00:01:53.185 --> 00:01:55.106
He was still gazing around in wonder.

27
00:01:55.126 --> 00:02:00.467
"I'll watch everything grow here," he announced, "and I'll grow too."

28
00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:03.328
"That's true," said Dickon.

29
00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.266
"We'll have you walking and digging soon."

30
00:02:06.286 --> 00:02:09.308
"Walking! Digging!

31
00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:11.209
Will I really do those things?"

32
00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.992
Dickon and Mary looked at each other.

33
00:02:15.313 --> 00:02:17.955
Neither of them had ever asked Colin about his legs.

34
00:02:19.176 --> 00:02:21.057
But it was as if he could read their minds.

35
00:02:21.077 --> 00:02:25.901
"Nothing is really wrong with my legs, but they're so thin and weak.

36
00:02:27.122 --> 00:02:30.085
They shake so much that I'm afraid to try to stand."

37
00:02:31.706 --> 00:02:34.148
Both Dickon and Mary breathed a sigh of relief.

38
00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:39.022
"When you stop being afraid," said Dickon, "then you'll stand.

39
00:02:40.282 --> 00:02:41.843
And you'll stop being afraid soon."

40
00:02:43.103 --> 00:02:44.884
They all sat quietly for a while.

41
00:02:46.024 --> 00:02:47.385
The sun was dropping lower.

42
00:02:48.565 --> 00:02:51.447
It was that hour of the day when everything stills itself.

43
00:02:53.147 --> 00:02:59.010
So in the midst of this stillness, it was rather alarming when Colin suddenly said, "Who is that

44
00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.531
man?" Dickon and Mary scrambled to their feet.

45
00:03:02.551 --> 00:03:05.360
"Man?" they cried.

46
00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:08.001
Colin pointed to the wall.

47
00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:11.022
"Look!" They turned around.

48
00:03:12.222 --> 00:03:15.723
There was Ben Weatherstaff glaring at them from the top of a ladder.

49
00:03:16.944 --> 00:03:18.524
He shook his fist at Mary.

50
00:03:18.544 --> 00:03:21.425
"I've never liked you!"

51
00:03:21.905 --> 00:03:22.425
he shouted.

52
00:03:22.445 --> 00:03:25.806
"You're always poking your nose where it's not wanted.

53
00:03:27.127 --> 00:03:30.407
If it hadn't been for that robin "Ben Weatherstaff!"

54
00:03:30.888 --> 00:03:31.988
Mary stood below him.

55
00:03:33.216 --> 00:03:34.937
"It was the robin who showed me the way."

56
00:03:36.257 --> 00:03:41.198
At this the old gardener seemed so outraged that Mary thought he was going to scramble down on

57
00:03:41.278 --> 00:03:42.199
her side of the wall.

58
00:03:42.219 --> 00:03:45.320
"You're a bad one.

59
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.740
Blaming the robin for what you did."

60
00:03:49.001 --> 00:03:51.901
While Ben kept scolding, Colin whispered to Dickon.

61
00:03:51.921 --> 00:03:53.282
"Wheel me over there."

62
00:03:54.482 --> 00:03:56.823
Ben's mouth dropped open at the sight of Colin.

63
00:03:56.843 --> 00:03:59.384
"Do you know who I am?"

64
00:03:59.864 --> 00:04:00.724
demanded Colin.

65
00:04:02.272 --> 00:04:04.074
Ben stared at the boy in the wheelchair.

66
00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:09.877
He passed his hands over his eyes, and when he answered, it was in a shaky voice.

67
00:04:09.897 --> 00:04:11.979
"Know who you are?

68
00:04:13.079 --> 00:04:15.381
With your mother's eyes staring out of your face?

69
00:04:16.582 --> 00:04:18.123
Of course I know who you are.

70
00:04:19.344 --> 00:04:22.726
You're that poor sick boy with the crooked back and legs."

71
00:04:24.307 --> 00:04:26.488
Colin turned bright red and sat up straight.

72
00:04:26.508 --> 00:04:29.570
"I don't have a crooked back and legs."

73
00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.732
"He doesn't!"

74
00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.381
said Mary angrily.

75
00:04:33.401 --> 00:04:37.083
"I've looked, and he doesn't have any lumps on his back."

76
00:04:38.284 --> 00:04:39.784
Ben kept staring at Colin.

77
00:04:40.965 --> 00:04:42.506
"You don't have a crooked back?

78
00:04:42.766 --> 00:04:43.987
You don't have crooked legs?"

79
00:04:45.608 --> 00:04:47.028
This was too much for Colin.

80
00:04:48.129 --> 00:04:52.211
The energy that he usually threw into his tantrums rushed through him in a new way.

81
00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:56.394
His anger and insulted pride filled him with strength.

82
00:04:57.794 --> 00:04:58.915
"Stand by my side!"

83
00:04:59.395 --> 00:05:02.197
he ordered Dickon, throwing the blankets off his legs.

84
00:05:03.477 --> 00:05:06.698
Dickon held Colin's arm as Colin put his feet on the ground.

85
00:05:06.718 --> 00:05:09.078
"He can do it!"

86
00:05:09.579 --> 00:05:10.259
Mary whispered.

87
00:05:11.539 --> 00:05:14.020
Then Colin was standing as straight as an arrow.

88
00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.920
"Look at me!"

89
00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:17.161
he said to Ben.

90
00:05:17.181 --> 00:05:18.921
"Just you look at me!"

91
00:05:18.941 --> 00:05:22.742
"He's as straight as I am," said Dickon.

92
00:05:24.043 --> 00:05:26.223
Mary couldn't believe what Ben did next.

93
00:05:27.544 --> 00:05:31.001
He choked and gulped, and tears ran down his cheeks.

94
00:05:31.021 --> 00:05:38.184
"When my father is away," said Colin, "I am your master, and you must obey me.

95
00:05:39.325 --> 00:05:40.725
This is my garden.

96
00:05:41.966 --> 00:05:43.727
Don't you dare say a word about it.

97
00:05:44.887 --> 00:05:46.588
Get down from that ladder at once.

98
00:05:47.949 --> 00:05:49.749
Mary will meet you and bring you to us."

99
00:05:49.769 --> 00:05:51.690
"Yes, sir!"

100
00:05:52.211 --> 00:05:54.952
said Ben, and he climbed down the ladder.
